# Sound — design.md §8's "sound", and §D7.9's audio backlog item, at the size a
# voxel game actually needs.
#
# **Procedural, like the atlas.** `client/atlas.gene` paints its textures rather
# than shipping PNGs, for reasons that apply here word for word: no asset to
# fetch, no load event, no file whose source nobody has. A dig is a noise burst
# and a place is a short tone, and both are three Web Audio nodes built and
# discarded per sound.
#
# §D7.9 puts a full `AudioContext` binding set "at the same tier as WebGL2",
# which is dozens of entries. What landed is two: `$audio/tone` and
# `$audio/noise`. A mod authoring music wants the graph; a game that needs a
# thud when you dig does not, and the graph can be added later without changing
# either of these.
#
# ## Why the context is created lazily
#
# A browser refuses to start an `AudioContext` before the user has interacted
# with the page, and a refused context is not an error — it is a context stuck
# in `suspended` that never plays anything. So the context is made on the first
# sound, which by construction is a click or a keypress.

(mod sound ^profile web)

# Pitches, in the small-interval range that reads as a game rather than a
# doorbell. A place is two quick notes a fifth apart; a dig is noise.
(let place_hz 523.25)
(let step_hz 784.0)

(fn new_sound [] : (List EventTarget)
  # A list rather than a nullable, because the profile has no nullable it can
  # narrow (see `client/net_main.gene`'s header on the same problem): an empty
  # list is "not yet", and a one-element list is the context.
  [])

(fn first_context [s : (List EventTarget)] : EventTarget
  (var i 0.0)
  s/%i)

(fn ensure_context [s : (List EventTarget)] : EventTarget
  (if_yes (== s/~size 0.0)
    (s ~ push! ($audio/context)))
  (first_context s))

(fn play_dig [s : (List EventTarget)] : Nil
  ($audio/noise (ensure_context s) 0.09 0.28))

(fn play_place [s : (List EventTarget)] : Nil
  ($audio/tone (ensure_context s) place_hz 0.06 0.16))

(fn play_craft [s : (List EventTarget)] : Nil
  (var ctx (ensure_context s))
  ($audio/tone ctx place_hz 0.05 0.14)
  ($audio/tone ctx step_hz 0.09 0.14))
